  "question": {
    "text": "Force between two point charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> placed in vacuum at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math> apart is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>. Force between them when placed in a medium having dielectric <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math> apart will be:",
